HISTORY_VERSION 1.0.0

TYPE Foundation

STATUS APPROVED

DATE 2026-07-06

TITLE

Minimal CLI implemented: pace init, pace doctor, pace context.

WHY

With Kernel, Services, Protocols and Contracts all real, the Dependency
Graph unblocked both Engines and CLI. Per the roadmap: a minimal CLI
wrapping the Kernel, starting with init, doctor and context.

DECISION

Implemented engines/project_creator.py's init_instance(): the Project
Creator engine's init mode only — attaches a valid, structurally minimal
.pace/ to an existing project directory. Writes placeholder mission,
vision, roadmap and sprint content (not just empty folders) precisely
because contracts/INSTANCE_CONTRACT_0.1.0.pdl's ROOT_MANIFEST requires
ACTIVE_MISSION/VISION/ROADMAP/SPRINT to be non-empty fields in
ACTIVE_VERSIONS.pdl — an instance cannot be structurally valid the
moment it's born unless those pointers already resolve to something
real.

While testing init_instance() against Doctor, found and fixed a real
bug: ORG_REF was being treated as unconditionally required (inherited
straight from the contract loader's flat field list), when the contract
actually marks it conditionally required — only when KIND=PROJECT,
absent when KIND=ORGANIZATION. The unconditional check silently
duplicated and contradicted the already-correct conditional check
sitting right below it. Caught because
test_init_organization_kind_does_not_require_org_ref failed on first
run, not assumed correct.

Implemented cli/pace.py: pace init (wraps init_instance, then runs
validate_instance and reports if the result isn't clean), pace doctor
(wraps validate_instance), pace context (reads INSTANCE.pdl and
ACTIVE_VERSIONS.pdl, prints identity plus the active mission/vision/
roadmap/sprint content inline). Not yet packaged as a real `pace`
executable — run as `python cli/pace.py <command>`; packaging is a later
decision, not part of this minimal CLI.

Verified end-to-end, not just unit-level: ran init -> doctor -> context
manually against a real temporary directory outside any test fixture,
confirmed clean output and exit codes. Also replaced a few em dashes in
CLI/Kernel print statements with plain hyphens after noticing one
render as a mojibake glyph in this terminal — a small, cheap fix against
exactly the class of Windows console-encoding bug already known from the
old system's emoji crashes, applied here proactively instead of waiting
to be bitten by it again.

Test count: kernel 5, contract loader 4, project creator 4, CLI 3 — 16
total, all passing before this commit.

IMPACT

PACE can now actually create a governed instance end-to-end from the
command line and confirm it's valid — the first time any of PACE's own
tooling has been used through its intended interface rather than called
as a library function in a test.

NEXT_STEPS

Per the roadmap: adopt TuPeríMetro as the first governed project (step
7), then implement pace create (step 8), then create the Plataforma de
Mantenimiento as the first new project born from PACE (step 9).

APPROVED_BY

President Cley Duarte

END
